 The gap addressed here is the joint treatment of ambiguous stationary sensing, shared-device attribution, and evidence-preserving conversational retrieval within this selected literature. This is a scoped integration contribution; it is not a claim that no prior system combines these features.
+
+The distinction is operational: the hydration comparison motivates an independent physical oracle (E1/E2), workplace interaction motivates a measured effort comparison (E4), and policy-oriented tool evaluation motivates subject isolation and repeated scoring (E5). Combining these concerns imposes session coordination and query-snapshot obligations that are specified below. This is our synthesis of the selected works, not evidence that those works lack every related mechanism.
